{
  "outcome": "patch",
  "candidate_reviews": {
    "C001": {
      "decision": "edit",
      "reason": "The constructor call uses the old field name `speed_mps` and must be updated to use the new unit (`speed_kph`) with a conversion factor of 3.6 (m/s → km/h)."
    },
    "C002": {
      "decision": "edit",
      "reason": "The output JSON key `speed_mps` in the `fields` dict must be renamed to `speed_kph`, and the value must be scaled by 3.6."
    },
    "C003": {
      "decision": "edit",
      "reason": "The speeding threshold check (`entity.speed_mps > 30.0`) must use the new unit (`speed_kph`) with a converted threshold (>108.0) and reference the correct field name."
    }
  },
  "edits": [
    {
      "before": "    sample = VehicleTelemetry(vehicle_id=request['vehicle_id'], speed_mps=request['speed'])\n",
      "after": "    sample = VehicleTelemetry(vehicle_id=request['vehicle_id'], speed_kph=float(request['speed']) * 3.6)\n"
    },
    {
      "before": "    fields = {'vehicle_id': entity.vehicle_id, 'speed_mps': entity.speed_mps}\n",
      "after": "    fields = {'vehicle_id': entity.vehicle_id, 'speed_kph': float(entity.speed_kph)}\n"
    },
    {
      "before": "    return {'fields': fields, 'speeding': entity.speed_mps > 30.0,\n",
      "after": "    return {'fields': fields, 'speeding': float(entity.speed_kph) > 108.0,\n"
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The schema change requires converting meters per second (m/s) to kilometers per hour (km/h) by multiplying by 3.6. All references to the old field name (`speed_mps`) must be updated to use `speed_kph`, and all speed comparisons must reflect the new unit's threshold (>108.0 km/h). The constructed payload uses the raw protobuf value, which is now in km/h due to the conversion logic. JSON output exposes exact decoded float32 values as numbers.",
  "confidence": 1.0,
  "assumptions": [
    "The input `request['speed']` is a numeric value representing meters per second (m/s) and can be safely multiplied by 3.6 without loss of precision.",
    "The protobuf-generated bindings preserve the float32 type for `speed_kph`, so no additional serialization/deserialization steps are needed beyond the conversion logic.",
    "The threshold check is strictly enforced as >108.0 km/h (previously >30.0 m/s).",
    "No mixed-unit scenarios exist during rollout; only the new unit is used in this runtime."
  ]
}
